{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520445906,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMDMyMDIzODc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2281","origin":"github"},"title":"remove --unregister-only ?","message":"#### What is the problem?\nNot clear (if possible) how to unlink a sub-dataset.  E.g. I have a dataset which I was to \"redo\", while keeping this current version somewhere for backup.  So the steps could be\n```\n  datalad remove -d . --unregister-only subds  # which does not remove it, just unlists from modules\n  mv subds newlocation/\n```\n\nfrom the docs it sounds like `git submodule deinit subds` should do it but it seems to not :-/:\n```shell\n$\u003e /usr/lib/git-annex.linux/git submodule deinit metasearch \nSubmodule work tree 'metasearch' contains a .git directory\n(use 'rm -rf' if you really want to remove it including all of its history)\n$\u003e git submodule\n+1d0a34d2debb14c77e2bfd47b62a193ca818add7 metasearch (heads/views/species=_;sex=_;site_id=_)\n```\nso no effect... didn't get an answer on git IRC on this question. @kyleam - do you know?\nfor now I just did something like `mv metasearch{,.aside}; mkdir metasearch; cd metasearch; git init; cd ..; datalad remove -d . metasearch`","files":null}]}